<title>FINLAND: NESTE IN TALKS WITH MANY ON BOREALIS STAKE - AGENCY.</title>
<headline>NESTE IN TALKS WITH MANY ON BOREALIS STAKE - AGENCY.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish oil group Neste Oy is in talks with several potential buyers of its half of petrochemicals group Borealis, Finnish STT news agency quoted Neste COO Jukka Viinanen as saying on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He was also quoted as saying that news on a deal should nonetheless not be expected soon. Norwegian state-owned Statoil owns the other half of Borealis.</p>
<p>Borealis said earlier its 1996 profit fell to a third of the 1995 level but that the final quarter marked a clear improvement. STT said the cyclical recovery would improve Borealis' attractiveness.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242</p>
